*> arithmetic_add_subtract.cbl -- demonstrates: ADD and SUBTRACT in both
*> their "TO"/"FROM" (accumulate in place) and "GIVING" (store in a new
*> field, leave operands unchanged) forms.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. ARITHADDSUB.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-ITEM-COUNT     PIC 9(4) VALUE 10.
01  WS-PRICE-A        PIC 9(4) VALUE 5.
01  WS-PRICE-B        PIC 9(4) VALUE 7.
01  WS-TOTAL-PRICE    PIC 9(4) VALUE 0.
01  WS-DISCOUNT       PIC 9(4) VALUE 3.
01  WS-REMAINING      PIC 9(4) VALUE 0.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    ADD 1 TO WS-ITEM-COUNT.
    DISPLAY "ITEM COUNT AFTER ADD: " WS-ITEM-COUNT.

    ADD WS-PRICE-A WS-PRICE-B GIVING WS-TOTAL-PRICE.
    DISPLAY "TOTAL PRICE: " WS-TOTAL-PRICE.

    SUBTRACT WS-DISCOUNT FROM WS-TOTAL-PRICE.
    DISPLAY "TOTAL AFTER DISCOUNT: " WS-TOTAL-PRICE.

    SUBTRACT 1 FROM WS-ITEM-COUNT GIVING WS-REMAINING.
    DISPLAY "REMAINING: " WS-REMAINING.
    STOP RUN.
